      "writtenOn": "2022-09-02T17:29:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not a blocking comment - if you moved the `usb_port` field from the mux `struct usb_mux` to the chain `struct usb_mux_chain`, does it simplify the macros and logic to determine the correct USB port number?\n\nFor example, `USB_MUX_CHAIN_STRUCT_INIT` would just add\n```\n.usb_port \u003d USBC_PORT_NEW(DT_PARENT(chain_id)),\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 321,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 321,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "cea1016d244dfe5c0e1d7fd77be18bd7800ea14a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b52d6a57_5a36b1c4",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/include/usbc/usb_muxes.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 321,
      "author": {
        "id": 1511343
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-06T07:59:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking about removing `usb_port` completely and passing it as argument to `usb_mux_driver` functions (e.g. `tcpm_drv` and `ppc_drv` has `port` argument in all functions). Probably code size would be reduced without having `usb_port` in each mux structure. The problem is with creating `bb_controls[]` (and other drivers that use `drv_controls[]` pattern and will be shimed), because it still needs `USB_MUX_PORT()` macro.",
      "parentUuid": "543a5e93_19ae0fc5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 321,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 321,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "cea1016d244dfe5c0e1d7fd77be18bd7800ea14a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a585ad5e_58bc4b70",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/include/usbc/usb_muxes.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 321,
      "author": {
        "id": 1511343
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-06T13:55:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I found the way to create `bb_controls[]` without implementing `USB_MUX_PORT()`. Macro would go for each chain looking for BB retimers. The `bb_controls_chain_x.retimer_rst_gpio` would be defined as `BB_RETIMER_RESET_GPIO(first_bb_id_in_chain_x) | BB_RETIMER_RESET_GPIO(second_bb_id_in_cahin_x) | 0`. This will evaluate to correct GPIO signal if all BB retimers in `chain_x` has the same configuration. Creating `BUILD_ASSERT` to check GPIO signal for BB retimers on the same mux is also possible to implement.\n\nThese BB macros should be simpler than `USB_MUX_PORT`.\n\nI am going to remove `usb_port`. Majority of drivers doesn\u0027t even use this property.",
      "parentUuid": "b52d6a57_5a36b1c4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 321,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 321,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "cea1016d244dfe5c0e1d7fd77be18bd7800ea14a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
